    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d624">

                <pb facs="0863" n="764" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg764"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.0145/18</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Boal</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 3646</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-06-03">June 3, 1936</date>.<lb/>[Received June
                        10.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    Department’s instruction No. 1110 of May 23, 1936 on the above-mentioned subject
                    and to enclose herewith a copy of the note which the Department directed the
                    Embassy to transmit to the Foreign Office.<anchor n="66" xml:id="d624-f1"/> It
                    will be observed that the Embassy’s note follows as closely as possible the
                    wording of the Department’s instruction.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pierre de L. Boal</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
